code/W104: A report entry names no item

A fact a report reader minted cites no item, because the report's file or line
lies in no collected item (a macro expansion, top-level statements, or a file no
source pack collected), or because an API snapshot's entry has a path no
collected item has: a re-exported path whose definition path differs, an item a
macro generates, or a crate whose library is named apart from its package. A
static finding is reported only when no collected package holds its file either,
or it has no location. The entry is kept with what the report says of it, so
nothing is lost. Collect the source pack for those files (`@rust/source`,
`@javascript/source`) and the manifest pack for their packages, then collect the
report again.

Owner: @code/core
Level: warning

code/W105: A finding's rule or level is unknown

A static finding's SARIF result states no rule (no `ruleId`, no `rule`, and no
rule index naming a rule of its tool's driver), or states no level (none on the
result, and none in its rule's `defaultConfiguration`): the field reads
`unknown`. The finding is kept, never dropped. SARIF's own default level is
`warning`; it is not applied, so a level the tool never wrote cannot pass for
one it did. Make the tool write its rule ids and levels in its SARIF output, or
the rule metadata (`tool.driver.rules` with a `defaultConfiguration.level`),
then collect the report again.

Owner: @code/core
Level: warning

code/W106: A dependency has no purl

A component of a CycloneDX bill of materials carries no package URL (`purl`), so
its dependency is named by name and version only
(`dep:<package>/@<name@version>`). The dependency is kept, never dropped, but no
other report can be matched to it: an OSV scan or another BOM names a package by
its purl. Generate the BOM with an SBOM tool that writes a purl for every
component (cargo-cyclonedx, cyclonedx-npm), then collect it again.

Owner: @code/core
Level: warning

code/W107: A vulnerability's severity is unknown

An OSV record of a vulnerability scan has no severity label
(`database_specific.severity`) and no CVSS v3 vector this reader rates: its only
severity entries are CVSS v4 or v2 vectors, or its v3 vector is malformed. The
vulnerability is kept with severity `unknown`, never dropped and never given a
guessed rating, so a gate on severity cannot pass it by mistake. Read the
advisory by its OSV id (osv.dev, or the database its id names) and judge its
severity there.

Owner: @code/core
Level: warning
